  "_note": "Baseline metrics snapshot the playtest skill diffs against (§13.2, #140). It is a snapshot of the --bot batch below on the commit named, one block PER PLAYSTYLE PROFILE (#198): a profile is a temperament, so each has its own numbers and they are never compared against each other as a leaderboard. It is SUPPOSED to drift: after any change expected to move the numbers (a tuning [START] knob, guard/vision/ability behaviour, generation, the bot policy itself, a profile's numbers), refresh it in the same PR with `./scripts/baseline.py --refresh` — never by hand, so every block moves together. That script also runs as a check on every PR (CI's `simbot baseline` job), re-running each block's own `command` and failing when a summary no longer matches: a stale baseline compared silently is the anti-pattern this file exists to avoid, and it is invisible unless something re-runs it. The per-profile `command` strings are what the check executes, so they are the authoritative description of what was measured; `config` below is the human-readable summary of them.",
